  at link  now  it's kind of like a leading indicator  you have to do a lot of other things you  can't study these words from wordless  you have to learn them through a lot of  listening and reading you also should  save phrases but the one easy thing  to measure the sort of gordy and not is  the number of words you know now people  are going to say well you know how do  you know if you know them you know them  passively you can't use them i don't  care  if i can understand them in a context  i'm happy because my goal is to  understand  and i know that if i build up my ability  to understand that's a very solid base  from which to start speaking if your  ability to speak gets ahead of your  ability to understand you'll be in for  some difficult times because you'll say  something and you won't understand what  people say back to you now in czech i've  been added since august link tells me  that i know 20 000 words i don't really  know 20 000 words  but i know that two months ago i only  know i only knew say ten thousand so now  i know twenty thousand so i know with  every day as i'm continuing to work at  it i am increasing my vocabulary and i  also know as i download text from  czech newspapers on the web that i  understand more and more of it that  there's more and more of these words  that in fact i do know albeit passively  so to me  a very good measure  of whether or not we're progressing  is this number of words that you know  uh because it means that your  comprehension is increasing whether in  fact it's 20 000 or because czech is a  very inflected language it equates to 5  000 words in english or whatever it  doesn't matter it's not for bragging  rights it's in order to  demonstrate to yourself that in fact you  are continuing to progress and if you  continue to progress and your vocabulary  you know the words known number  continues to increase you will  understand better and better you'll read  more material you'll as you're reading  you'll come across so