 a lot more listening  and then i'm going to start speaking  more i've spoken a couple of times it's  been very difficult but i'm quite  convinced that some other people who  maybe start speaking earlier will be  ahead of me it's a bit of a sort of  tortoise and hair situation the hair  will jump ahead of me they'll be able to  say more things and check  very early but in the long run after six  months i'm convinced that i will be able  to do more with my check  in terms of reading listening having  intelligent conversations with people on  a variety of subjects  so  there's a quickie then on  and that's a theme that i've i've talked  about before  and that is you know now i've got to  find where is it  i've got to find my cursor uh  yeah words keep up your word count and  you'll get there that is the as i've  described before it's the basically the  little uh mechanical rabbit at the dog  race it's something that keeps you going  so  thank you for listening oh and i should  add that obviously these words have to  be gleaned through things that you enjoy  doing so listening to music if you like  in songs or listening to  um audiobooks or reading  you know books or articles but  constantly pushing yourself a little  further and further ahead and increasing  your known word count thank you for  listening bye for now

